# Vercel picks a runtime by sniffing the repo, and this is a static site - the
# build just regenerates docs/topics.js and Vercel serves the folder.
#
# Without these two lines it finds server.py in its entrypoint list and tries
# to run the repo as a Python serverless function, which fails the build with
# "No python entrypoint found". server.py is for Render, where a long-running
# process makes sense; on Vercel there is no server to run.
server.py

# Only the topic scripts need matplotlib/scipy/jupyter. build_site.py is
# stdlib, and leaving this visible is the other half of the runtime sniffing.
requirements.txt
